WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Cooling and heat. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Trace heat paths and thermal limits

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: A cooling system transfers heat away from hot components and rejects it to the surroundings. Flow, area and temperature difference all matter.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Draw a closed path from hot part through coolant and radiator to ambient air; arrows should form one continuous loop.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Energy-flow map

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Trace heat paths and thermal limits
